PART 2 — PROJECT EVOLUTION LOG (March 2026)
================================================================================

Phase 1: Initial Setup & Upload
────────────────────────────────
- Created GitHub repository: https://github.com/fragilepotato/mode-5 (master branch)
- Uploaded initial MATLAB files:
    • demo_comm.m         — Mode 5 IFF challenge-response system
    • reset_zedboard_ip.m — ZedBoard IP configuration via serial (COM8, 115200 baud)
    • slow_simulation_IFF.m — ZedBoard-only loopback test
    • test5.m             — Early test script

Phase 2: Mode 5 IFF Implementation (demo_comm.m v1)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- Rewrote demo_comm.m with full Mode 5 IFF features:
    • BPSK + DSSS modulation (Gold code, length-31 PN sequence)
    • HMAC-style MAC with pre-shared 16-byte key
    • CRC-16 validation
    • Two-phase protocol: 1030 MHz interrogation, 1090 MHz reply
    • 5-cycle continuous operation at 5-second intervals
    • Live monitor figure with I/Q, spectrum, and status display
- Result: FAILED — 5 compounding bugs described in Part 1 above

Phase 3: ADS-B Baseline Test (test_adsb_link.m)
────────────────────────────────────────────────
- Created test_adsb_link.m — simplified ADS-B PPM test to validate RF link
- Purpose: strip away Mode 5 complexity, test bare hardware link first
- Features:
    • Auto gain calibration sweep (3 settings)
    • 12 MSPS (corrected from 4 MSPS)
    • movmean DC removal (replaced broken highpass approach)
    • PlutoSDR complex signal fix (sig + 1i*1e-12)
    • 5-cycle test with live BER plots
- Result: PERFECT MATCH — 0 bit errors across all 5 cycles
- This was the FIRST SUCCESSFUL COMMUNICATION

Phase 4: demo_comm.m Rebuilt with Lessons Learned
─────────────────────────────────────────────────
- Rewrote demo_comm.m incorporating all 5 bug fixes:
    • fs = 12 MSPS (was 4 MSPS)
    • BPSK modulation with known preamble (no DSSS, no Gold code)
    • movmean DC removal on real(IQ) (no highpass)
    • CRC-16 only (MAC removed temporarily for incremental testing)
    • Complex xcorr phase recovery for carrier phase ambiguity
    • Polarity-tolerant BPSK demodulator
- Frame formats:
    • Interrogation: [Sync16][Type8][ID16][Challenge32][CRC16] = 88 bits
    • Reply: [Sync16][Type8][ID16][Challenge32][IFF24][CRC16] = 112 bits
- BPSK demodulator key innovation:
    • xcorr(complex_rx, real_preamble) → abs() for phase-invariant peak detection
    • angle(c(peak)) recovers unknown carrier phase θ between TX/RX LOs
    • rx_rotated = rx * exp(-jθ) → real() gives clean ±1 BPSK symbols
    • This solves the LO phase ambiguity problem inherent in separate oscillators

Phase 5: Split into Ground Station + Aircraft Transponder
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- Split test_adsb_link.m into two separate scripts for proper IFF protocol:

### test_adsb_pluto.m — IFF Ground Station (ADALM Pluto)
    Role: Interrogator
    Step 1: TX interrogation on 1030 MHz
        Frame: [DF=B0][StationID=1A2B][Mode=05][Challenge=D2CE21DA][CRC]
        Hold TX for 3.0 seconds
    Step 2: Switch to RX on 1090 MHz
        Listen for up to 6.0 seconds for aircraft reply
    Step 3: Decode reply → extract ICAO address → report identification
    Output: "AIRCRAFT 4840D6 IDENTIFIED" or "NO REPLY"

### test_adsb_zedboard.m — IFF Aircraft Transponder (ZedBoard FMCOMMS3)
    Role: Transponder (runs autonomously — no PC console needed)
    Step 1: Listen on 1030 MHz for interrogation
        Validates DF=B0 sync header
        Extracts ground station ID, mode code, challenge nonce
    Step 2: Build reply with aircraft identity
        Frame: [DF=8D][ICAO=4840D6][Squawk/IFF data][Challenge echo][CRC]
    Step 3: TX reply on 1090 MHz (hold 4.0 seconds)
    Confirmation: The RF reply IS the confirmation — ground station decodes it

    IP Core Candidate Functions (for Vivado 2023.2 / HDL Coder):
        adsb_preprocess()   — envelope + movmean DC removal
                               HDL: sliding-window accumulator
        adsb_framesync()    — bipolar preamble matched filter (96-tap)
                               HDL: FIR with ROM coefficients
        adsb_decode_bits()  — PPM half-period energy comparator
                               HDL: adder + comparator (no divider)

Phase 5 Protocol Flow:
    Ground Station (Pluto)              Aircraft (ZedBoard)
    ──────────────────                  ───────────────────
    TX interrogation 1030 MHz ────────► RX + validate DF=B0
                                         Build reply with ICAO
    RX on 1090 MHz ◄──────────────────  TX reply 1090 MHz
    Decode → ICAO = 4840D6
    "AIRCRAFT IDENTIFIED"

Run Order: ZedBoard first (starts listening), then Pluto (sends interrogation).

