================================================================================
KNOWN ISSUES & TROUBLESHOOTING
================================================================================

1. "Failed to create context for uri: ip:192.168.1.10"
   → ZedBoard IP not set. Run reset_zedboard_ip.m first.
   → Check: PC Ethernet adapter at 192.168.1.x, subnet 255.255.255.0
   → Verify: ping 192.168.1.10

2. "Input X must be complex"
   → PlutoSDR rejects real waveform. Ensure TX uses: sig + 1i*1e-12

3. BER = 50% with high SNR
   → LO phase ambiguity. Use complex xcorr for phase recovery (demo_comm.m)
   → Or use envelope-based PPM decoder (test_adsb_*.m) which is phase-invariant

4. All 1-bits decoded as 0 (exactly N errors = N ones in message)
   → highpass() on envelope. Replace with movmean DC removal.

5. ADC clipping (max > 1.0)
   → Reduce TX gain or RX gain. For SMA cable: TX=-20, RX=+10.

6. Timing: "NO REPLY" despite both devices working
   → Start ZedBoard script FIRST (it listens), then Pluto (it transmits).
   → ZedBoard listen window = 15 s per cycle. Start Pluto within that window.